<Base title="About" description="On Simplicity is an independent publication about simple living, home and everyday life, alongside a directory of Resource Partners." breadcrumbs={[{name:'Home',path:'/'},{name:'About'}]}><header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">A little less. A little better.</p><h1>Room for what matters.</h1><p>Simple living for real life, not a life arranged for a photograph.</p></header><article class="prose prose-stone max-w-none reading-width"><h2>A practical kind of simplicity</h2><p>On Simplicity is an independent publication about the ordinary choices that shape a day: what comes into a home, how work gets done, where money goes and how people make time for one another. We believe a useful idea should meet you where you are. It should not require a perfect home, an empty calendar or a completely different personality.</p><p>Our journal covers <a href="/category/simple-living/">simple living</a>, <a href="/category/organization/">home and organizing</a>, money, relationships, well-being and personal growth. The emphasis is on specific, manageable changes. That might mean making the laundry routine less frustrating, reconsidering an expensive habit or finding a clearer way to say no. Some ideas will fit your circumstances; others will not. Taking what helps is part of the point.</p><h2>Familiar topics, fresh writing</h2><p>The name On Simplicity has a history as a simple-living blog. This publication is a new editorial project, not a continuation of its original author’s personal story. Selected familiar article addresses have been retained so that readers following older links can still find useful discussion of the subjects they expected. The writing at those addresses is new, and the displayed publication dates refer to this edition.</p><p>Titles that mention personal experiences are retained as historical titles, not claims that our editorial team had those experiences. We do not reproduce the former author’s articles or present invented memories as evidence. You can browse the current collection in the <a href="/archives/">archives</a>, organized by subject rather than by the dates in older addresses.</p><h2>Finding practical help</h2><p>Not every task is best handled alone. Our <a href="/resource-partners/">Resource Partners directory</a> introduces independent businesses and provides space for their service and project articles. Directory information and contributed articles should be treated as starting points for research, not independent certification or a promise of results. Availability, credentials, prices and suitability should always be checked directly with the business.</p><h2>Our editorial approach</h2><p>We aim for clear language, realistic suggestions and a distinction between general information and individual advice. Health, money and relationship topics can involve circumstances an article cannot know. Seek qualified help when a decision calls for it, and never feel obliged to simplify away support you need. A simpler life is not a competition. It is a little more room to pay attention to your own.</p></article></Base>
